=== OEM easy installation ===

This device can be flashed using the OEM web interface firmware upgrade mechanism. 

  * Navigate to Management -> System Manager -> Firmware
  * Under //Firmware Upgrade// select **Browse** choose the ''...netgear_wax220-squashfs-factory.img'' image file then press **Upload**
  * The file size of exactly 10MB is to bypass a minimal size check of the web interface. You can check the successful upload by comparing the MD5 checksum.
  * Press **Proceed** to start the firmware upgrade to OpenWrt!
  * Flashing takes about 20 seconds. Note that the OEM web interface won't realize the change to OpenWrt, hence your browser will be stuck at firmware flashing screen (continuously showing "Waiting for changes to be applied..."). 
  * If the power LED started flashing but the LAN LED is powered off and you cannot access the 192.168.1.1, power cycle the router.
  * When both power LED is flashing and LAN LED is on, simply [[docs:guide-quick-start:walkthrough_login|Log into your router running OpenWrt]] as normal.


=== OEM installation using the TFTP method ===

->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp]]

  * Download the OpenWrt initramfs image. Copy the image to a TFTP server and rename it to `openwrt.bin`
  * Connect the TFTP server to the WAX220. Conect to the serial console, interrupt the autoboot process by pressing '0' when prompted.
  * Download & Boot the OpenWrt initramfs image.

    $ setenv ipaddr 192.168.2.1
    $ setenv serverip 192.168.2.2
    $ tftpboot openwrt.bin
    $ bootm

  * Wait for OpenWrt to boot. Transfer the sysupgrade image to the device using scp and install using sysupgrade.

    $ sysupgrade -n <path-to-recovery.itb>

